<title>HONG KONG: HK's Western Harbour Tunnel to open on April 30.</title>
<headline>HK's Western Harbour Tunnel to open on April 30.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The third tunnel under Hong Kong's harbour will begin operation on April 30, the chairman of the Western Harbour Tunnel Co Ltd said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Robert Adams said the opening was three months ahead of schedule.</p>
<p>The HK$7.5 billion tunnel, one of the 10 Airport Core Projects, is two kilometres long and will link Hong Kong island's Western district with west Kowloon, from where an expressway will link it to the new Chek Lap Kok airport.</p>
<p>The toll charge for the tunnel is to be HK$30.</p>
<p>Western Harbour Tunnel Co is 37 percent owned by the Cross-Harbour Tunnel Co Ltd and 35 percent by CITIC Pacific Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
